  "id": "treatment-seeking-behavior",
  "term": "treatment-seeking behavior",
  "definition": "Treatment-seeking behavior is the way people pursue care when they are ill, including use of professional health services as well as traditional or indigenous remedies. In this source, it refers to how those choices can affect whether illness is effectively controlled or may persist or recur.",
